//! The sqe dispatch seam (P2-1): plan-tree recognition → engine lowering
//! → engine execution → typed DestReceiver output. R1 semantics: once a
//! statement addresses a pgrcolumnar2 relation there is NO fallback —
//! the engine answers it or the statement fails with a typed, censused
//! ERROR (`refusal::Refusal::into_error`). Heap statements never enter
//! (the caller's AM walk exits on first mismatch).
//!
//! Mechanism lineage (dispatch.md; lanev4 lx4seam carried on the
//! mechanisms, none of the lx4 lattice): the already-opened-relations AM
//! walk; the run-class gates ahead of recognition; recognize-aggref /
//! cmp-conjunct plan walks (M4-S4 full-width commuted-const law); the
//! reused-virtual-slot DestReceiver delivery with per-row cfi; ea_start/
//! ea_stop honest EXPLAIN ANALYZE stamping (WW-3). The `Vec<String>`
//! ABI dies at this seam: answers arrive as the engine's typed
//! `AnswerSet` and leave as descriptor-typed datums.

